{"Title":"An Act relative to cannabis advertisements by out of state dispensaries","BillNumber":"H3559","DocketNumber":"HD3122","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"MSV1","Name":"Marcus S. Vaughn","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MSV1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T09:36:27.53"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"MSV1","Name":"Marcus S. Vaughn","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MSV1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T09:36:27.53"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3559/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Vaughn of Wrentham, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3559) of Marcus S. Vaughn relative to cannabis advertisements by out of state dispensaries.  Cannabis Policy.","DocumentText":"\tSection 4 of chapter 94G of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the word “health”, in line 266, the following words:- ; (15) a prohibition on advertising by dispensaries that operate exclusively outside of the commonwealth.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J50","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J50"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}